    <Notes ShowOnLoad="1" Notes="HexNode v03 small wall (row 1: 3 nodes, row 2: 2 nodes), 1.8 mm acrylic: a +5V strip (14 mm) and a GND strip (20 mm) per row, stacked bottom to top as row 1 +5V, row 1 GND, row 2 +5V, row 2 GND; 2 rail gauges for 2 rows. Odd rows (1, 3, ...) and even rows (2, 4, ...) are different strips: even-row nodes sit half a node pitch (38 mm) along. All strips share the LEFT end: line the rows up on a straight edge at the left, then space them with the rail gauges. Each end has a 3.2 mm hole for an M3 screw + ring lug (run the copper tape over both holes) and the polarity engraved beyond it. Layer order: engrave labels (fill), inner cuts (magnet pockets, terminal holes), outlines. Set power and speed for your laser on all three layers."/>
